&lt;p&gt;Answer : &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Just like the Dumpster challenge, I quickly open the image file given using  Exterro FTK Imager. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/siber-siaga-2025-preliminary/img-02.png"
width="401"
height="397"
srcset="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/siber-siaga-2025-preliminary/img-02.png 401w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 800px, 100vw"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Screenshot 2"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="101"
data-flex-basis="242px"
&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I found out there were multiple interesting file directories, and when for looking.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/siber-siaga-2025-preliminary/img-03.png"
width="593"
height="255"
srcset="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/siber-siaga-2025-preliminary/img-03_hu_5faf568b5f8b3f45.png 480w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/siber-siaga-2025-preliminary/img-03.png 593w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 800px, 100vw"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Screenshot 3"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="232"
data-flex-basis="558px"
&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the explorer folder, I noticed there are multiple deleted files. So I try to export them to my laptop and try to see it using tools named Thumb cache viewer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/siber-siaga-2025-preliminary/img-04.png"
width="1600"
height="904"
srcset="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/siber-siaga-2025-preliminary/img-04_hu_676faeeafd434928.png 480w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/siber-siaga-2025-preliminary/img-04_hu_18e5e3dbbf8b3b91.png 1024w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/siber-siaga-2025-preliminary/img-04.png 1600w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 800px, 100vw"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Screenshot 4"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="176"
data-flex-basis="424px"
&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I check every single file and I see the flag in an image. Then I merged all the info from all the images and got the flag.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flag = SIBER25{V3RY_sMA1L_thUm8n411S}&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>SUN CTF 2025: Who's Alpha</title><link>https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/</link><pubDate>Mon, 25 Aug 2025 09:14:47 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/1.jpg" alt="Featured image of post SUN CTF 2025: Who's Alpha" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;Chall details&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Field&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Details&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Author&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;warlocksmurf &amp;amp; Sai&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Category&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;OSINT&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Score&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;260&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;One of the largest financial institutions in Malaysia, &lt;strong&gt;MoneyPro Sdn Bhd&lt;/strong&gt;, has been breached by a notorious hacker group led by a mysterious figure known only as “Alpha.” As part of the &lt;strong&gt;Malaysia Cyber Defend Associate (MCDA)&lt;/strong&gt; team, your mission is to uncover Alpha’s true identity. Flag format: &lt;code&gt;sunctf25{Firstname_LastName}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Interestingly this chall only had 4 out of 81 teams that were able to solve it in time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The challenge shipped with an incident report on the MoneyPro breach: &lt;a class="link" href="investigation-report.pdf" &gt;Investigation Report (PDF)&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id="-solution"&gt;&lt;a href="#-solution" class="header-anchor"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;🕵️‍♂️ Solution
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;From the &lt;a class="link" href="https://github.com/Rizzykun/rizzykun.github.io/blob/master/content/post/2025/sunctf/osint/InvesigationReport.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;Investigation Report&lt;/a&gt; given,
The only lead we have is the social media account of a user named &lt;strong&gt;Bravo&lt;/strong&gt;. That’s where the OSINT trail begins..&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/1.jpg"
width="794"
height="717"
srcset="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/1_hu_793e0eafeb50a87.jpg 480w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/1.jpg 794w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 800px, 100vw"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Image1"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="110"
data-flex-basis="265px"
&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id="tracking-bravos-social-media"&gt;&lt;a href="#tracking-bravos-social-media" class="header-anchor"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Tracking Bravo’s Social Media
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I searched through popular social platforms and eventually located Bravo’s &lt;strong&gt;X (Twitter)&lt;/strong&gt; account.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/2.png"
width="1124"
height="871"
srcset="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/2_hu_1f382a9bbb463aaf.png 480w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/2_hu_92157f728a7c4ff2.png 1024w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/2.png 1124w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 800px, 100vw"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Image2"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="129"
data-flex-basis="309px"
&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scrolling through his timeline revealed an interesting clue—a suspicious &lt;strong&gt;Google Drive link&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/3.png"
width="1220"
height="686"
srcset="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/3_hu_bf80bfbcfb99afc4.png 480w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/3_hu_93fde82254107e46.png 1024w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/3.png 1220w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 800px, 100vw"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Image3"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="177"
data-flex-basis="426px"
&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id="exploring-the-google-drive"&gt;&lt;a href="#exploring-the-google-drive" class="header-anchor"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Exploring the Google Drive
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Drive contained:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A folder full of &lt;strong&gt;logos&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A file named &lt;code&gt;Private.zip&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &lt;code&gt;Note.txt&lt;/code&gt; file&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/4.png"
width="1172"
height="163"
srcset="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/4_hu_74eeaaa9a3f97654.png 480w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/4_hu_83cf90fbbb5deda2.png 1024w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/4.png 1172w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 800px, 100vw"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Image4"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="719"
data-flex-basis="1725px"
&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Opening the note revealed a &lt;strong&gt;password hint&lt;/strong&gt;: it was a combination of Bravo’s mother’s name and an important day (the day he signed a &lt;strong&gt;RM10,000 contract&lt;/strong&gt;). Both details can be found in his X posts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id="unlocking-the-zip"&gt;&lt;a href="#unlocking-the-zip" class="header-anchor"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Unlocking the Zip
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/5.png"
width="661"
height="188"
srcset="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/5_hu_247964f2db27f9a9.png 480w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/5.png 661w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 800px, 100vw"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Image5"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="351"
data-flex-basis="843px"
&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With the password reconstructed, I unzipped &lt;code&gt;Private.zip&lt;/code&gt; to find intelligence on the &lt;strong&gt;TigerP4tch&lt;/strong&gt; group. Inside Bravo’s folder, I finally uncovered a partial name:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lucas M.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The hunt for his last name was on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id="following-charlies-trail"&gt;&lt;a href="#following-charlies-trail" class="header-anchor"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Following Charlie’s Trail
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Inside Charlie’s folder, a chat log between Bravo and Charlie revealed another breadcrumb. Bravo hinted that something important was stored on &lt;strong&gt;Pastebin&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/6.png"
width="1440"
height="3200"
srcset="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/6_hu_d5eb90a78808bb1.png 480w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/6_hu_c9f22be7608af493.png 1024w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/6.png 1440w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 800px, 100vw"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Image6"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="45"
data-flex-basis="108px"
&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id="pastebin-recon"&gt;&lt;a href="#pastebin-recon" class="header-anchor"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Pastebin Recon
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;After some digging, I located a Pastebin account under the username &lt;code&gt;Alice_R&lt;/code&gt;. However, the paste was &lt;strong&gt;password-protected&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/7.png"
width="1264"
height="388"
srcset="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/7_hu_e1af687b82eb60ea.png 480w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/7_hu_884b9cec9a305959.png 1024w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/7.png 1264w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 800px, 100vw"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Image7"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="325"
data-flex-basis="781px"
&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Back in the Google Drive folder full of logos, I noticed Alice’s shop logo featuring a &lt;strong&gt;rose&lt;/strong&gt;. The chat log mentioned the password is the flower on her shop logo. Trying &lt;strong&gt;rose&lt;/strong&gt; as the password worked, unlocking the paste.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/8.png"
width="896"
height="613"
srcset="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/8_hu_444e05c880d7bd82.png 480w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/osint-whos-alpha/8.png 896w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 800px, 100vw"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Image8"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="146"
data-flex-basis="350px"
&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id="the-final-reveal"&gt;&lt;a href="#the-final-reveal" class="header-anchor"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;The Final Reveal
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The unlocked paste finally exposed Alpha’s full name:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lucas Moore&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With that, Alpha’s identity was confirmed.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>WHY CTF 2025: Shoe Shop</title><link>https://rizzykun.github.io/p/web-shoe-shop/</link><pubDate>Mon, 25 Aug 2025 09:14:47 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://rizzykun.github.io/p/web-shoe-shop/</guid><description>&lt;img src="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/web-shoe-shop/shoeshop.png" alt="Featured image of post WHY CTF 2025: Shoe Shop" /&gt;&lt;h2 id="-description"&gt;&lt;a href="#-description" class="header-anchor"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;📝 Description
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;We just launched a brand-new &lt;a class="link" href="https://shoe-shop-1.ctf.zone/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
&gt;shoe store&lt;/a&gt; to sell some fancy kicks.
Unfortunately, the admin beat us to it and already snagged the &lt;strong&gt;exclusive pair&lt;/strong&gt; in his cart. 👟✨
But hey—feel free to explore the shop, try out the cart, and see what you can uncover.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 id="-solution-walkthrough"&gt;&lt;a href="#-solution-walkthrough" class="header-anchor"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;💡 Solution Walkthrough
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;We’re dealing with an online shoe store where you can:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sign up for an account&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Add items to your cart&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;View your cart contents&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pretty normal e-commerce flow, right? Or… is it? 👀&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/web-shoe-shop/shoeshop.png"
width="1914"
height="833"
srcset="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/web-shoe-shop/shoeshop_hu_5e3ff98f48a94def.png 480w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/web-shoe-shop/shoeshop_hu_ddd4484ee0fb2d9e.png 1024w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/web-shoe-shop/shoeshop.png 1914w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 800px, 100vw"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Image1"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="229"
data-flex-basis="551px"
&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3 id="-the-idor-moment"&gt;&lt;a href="#-the-idor-moment" class="header-anchor"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;🔓 The IDOR Moment
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;While browsing the cart, something caught my eye…
The URL looked like this:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;page=cart&amp;amp;id=694&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt; parameter smells suspicious. What if we tweak it? 🤔&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So let’s try checking &lt;strong&gt;id #1 cart&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;https://shoe-shop-1.ctf.zone/index.php?page=cart&amp;amp;id=1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bingo! 🎯 We just accessed another user’s cart. And guess who that is? Yep—the admin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/web-shoe-shop/shoeshop2.png"
width="694"
height="206"
srcset="https://rizzykun.github.io/p/web-shoe-shop/shoeshop2_hu_b184b87d3a10fd29.png 480w, https://rizzykun.github.io/p/web-shoe-shop/shoeshop2.png 694w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 800px, 100vw"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="336"
data-flex-basis="808px"
&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3 id="-flag"&gt;&lt;a href="#-flag" class="header-anchor"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;🏁 Flag
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;And there it is:
&lt;code&gt;flag{00f34f9c417fcaa72b16f79d02d33099}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⚡Lesson learned: &lt;strong&gt;Always validate user access before showing sensitive data.&lt;/strong&gt;🚨&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>